1aky|n|One who admonishes; one who warns of faults, informs of duty, or gives advice and instruction by way of reproof or caution. ; Hence, specifically, a pupil selected to look to the school in the absence of the instructor, to notice the absence or faults of the scholars, or to instruct a division or class. ; Any large Old World lizard of the genus Varanus; esp., the Egyptian species (V. Niloticus), which is useful because it devours the eggs and young of the crocodile. It is sometimes five or six feet long. ; An ironclad war vessel, very low in the water, and having one or more heavily-armored revolving turrets, carrying heavy guns. ; A tool holder, as for a lathe, shaped like a low turret, and capable of being revolved on a vertical pivot so as to bring successively the several tools in holds into proper position for cutting.	a:mgb,43,1326;23ta,39,76;1ket,24,40;qkz,22,4;19iy,22,71;19t2,19,5;5nq,18,4;21ut,17,41;pj0,17,3;12l0,14,199;21gw,11,2;id5,10,4;ql0,10,239;25m4,9,90;1r2i,8,4~mgb,43,1326;ql0,10,239;12l0,14,199;1tq5,7,158;25m4,9,90;23ta,39,76;19iy,22,71;21ut,17,41;1ket,24,40;7mq,6,31;1t2w,5,27;1lpk,5,11;ak7,3,11;r72,5,9;20sq,7,5	v:bqp,23,3;237i,17,8;19uv,15,2;a6l,14,3;jgt,13,4;6ks,12,200;232k,5,49;u2v,2,6;jhd,1,5~6ks,12,200;232k,5,49;237i,17,8;u2v,2,6;jhd,1,5;jgt,13,4;a6l,14,3;bqp,23,3;19uv,15,2	V:7yv,31,3;17zy,29,9;1lf9,16,3;81e,16,3;k7c,14,3;1r2i,11,5;4my,9,2;1xlk,8,5;19t2,6,2;ydo,6,6;1q7n,5,4;19t3,4,3;1sam,2,4;232k,1,39;lg4,1,2~232k,1,39;17zy,29,9;ydo,6,6;1r2i,11,5;1xlk,8,5;s7u,0,4;1sam,2,4;1q7n,5,4;k7c,14,3;81e,16,3;19t3,4,3;1lf9,16,3;7yv,31,3;lg4,1,2;19t2,6,2	n:wu,74,5343;emk,64,15;iom,41,427;1t43,41,1180;1i81,34,16;1aky,30,880;226c,28,108;20f9,26,3469;1prv,23,14;1pwu,21,92;mi1,21,3;1czc,19,28;1kgq,18,7;1gy1,15,3;154f,12,11~wu,74,5343;20f9,26,3469;1t43,41,1180;1aky,30,880;jma,10,616;iom,41,427;edl,0,165;226c,28,108;2168,10,94;1pwu,21,92;1pvx,4,70;20hb,11,30;1czc,19,28;x1z,3,18;1i81,34,16	N:7zp,43,10;1aky,30,880;1pvx,28,362;4mz,28,28;hmu,23,8;fjk,23,8;a6m