1auf|n|A large cervine mammal (Alces machlis, or A. Americanus), native of the Northern United States and Canada. The adult male is about as large as a horse, and has very large, palmate antlers. It closely resembles the European elk, and by many zoologists is considered the same species. See Elk.	a:9ki,114,2~9ki,114,2	v:1249,19,3~1249,19,3	V:9ef,72,2~9ef,72,2	n:1ctv,182,9~1ctv,182,9
