1auh|n|A ring for gauging wooden pins. ; A meeting for discussion and deliberation; esp., a meeting of the people of a village or district, in Anglo-Saxon times, for the discussion and settlement of matters of common interest; -- usually in composition; as, folk-moot. ; of Mot	a:1pgd,51,1;6qx,6,1;7wi,4,3;165x,2,2~7wi,4,3;165x,2,2;1pgd,51,1;6qx,6,1	v:1pgd,51,1;6qx,6,1~1pgd,51,1;6qx,6,1	n:1jvx,16,7;13gh,6,4;1njd,1,5~1jvx,16,7;1njd,1,5;13gh,6,4	N:3r0,48,2;1jvx,11,5~1jvx,11,5;3r0,48,2
